Z||000000||Eric||02-09-2001||11:57 PM||||Everytime I first move the car after it has been parked for a while, I hear a clunk.  It's coming from the front end, and it only does it when I first move, kind of like something settled out of place then magically realigned itself after I forced it into place.  My guess it the ball joints are worn.  What's yours?<P>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||MontanaFiero||02-10-2001||02:14 AM||||Could be worn caliper bushings. that would cause the caliper to shift slightly and "clunk"; perhaps only when you are beginning to back up, but it doesn't hit anything hard when you are going forward.<P>Take the tire off and try to move the calipers in all direction. Also do this with the hub (bearings?),  and the knuckle (with a pry bar).<P>------------------<BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- project &lt;&lt;||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jake||02-10-2001||07:37 AM||||My Rx-7 will do the same thing. The clunk comes from the back tho...and it will only do it if the e-brake was on while it was sitting. Alot of mazda's are kinda known for it. My guess would be the brake calipers also. ||||reg||6
Z||000003||2birds||02-11-2001||12:05 AM||||Mine did that once when the alignment shop technichian didn't tighten the bolts on my upper balljoints.||||reg||1
